{
  spec: "§8.2"
  description: "The pairing vector for the two refusals: mechanism 1 is a relation over a set, so it fires on a colliding pair and never on a lone name. A Cyrillic field name with nothing to collide with is read like any other, which is the half a processor must not over-refuse -- §8.2 says 'id_пользователя alone is not' caught."
  valid: {
    value: {
      record: {
        fields: [
          {
            name: "аdmin"
            value: { atom: { number: "1" } }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
